WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:07.530
After a busy day, slowing down can take a little transition time.

2
00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:13.634
A wind-down gives you a quieter space between the demands of the day and

3
00:00:13.634 --> 00:00:14.070
bedtime.

4
00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:15.950
It can be simple.

5
00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:22.256
You might lower the lights, put demanding work aside, or choose a quiet

6
00:00:22.256 --> 00:00:23.711
activity you enjoy.

7
00:00:24.131 --> 00:00:29.457
Reading a few pages, listening to gentle audio, or preparing something for

8
00:00:29.457 --> 00:00:32.121
tomorrow could fit into your evening.

9
00:00:32.121 --> 00:00:36.604
Choose one change that feels realistic for your circumstances.

10
00:00:37.024 --> 00:00:42.109
Sleep is influenced by many things, including timing, light, noise, health,

11
00:00:42.109 --> 00:00:47.194
caffeine, and alcohol. A regular schedule and a suitable sleeping environment

12
00:00:47.194 --> 00:00:49.506
can also help support sleep.

13
00:00:49.506 --> 00:00:53.667
But a wind-down cannot guarantee when you’ll fall asleep.

14
00:00:54.087 --> 00:01:00.889
Try approaching it as an invitation to slow down, rather than a test you need

15
00:01:00.889 --> 00:01:01.797
to pass.

16
00:01:01.797 --> 00:01:08.339
If an activity leaves you more alert or frustrated, you can adjust it. You

17
00:01:08.339 --> 00:01:14.415
don’t have to keep a routine simply because it works for someone else.

18
00:01:14.835 --> 00:01:19.455
Tonight, consider one small way to make the evening gentler.

19
00:01:19.455 --> 00:01:24.993
You’re creating conditions that may support rest. You don’t have to control

20
00:01:24.993 --> 00:01:26.377
the exact result.
